    {
      "id": "library/dspace-7-rest-contract/blocks/prose-s032-refresh-authentication",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Refresh authentication",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s032-refresh-authentication.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### Refresh authentication\nTokens are only valid for a configurable amount of time (see below). When a token is about to expire (the timestamp provided in the exp claim, see below), you can request a new token with a new expiration time (by default 30 minutes). To do so send the token using the Header `Authorization: Bearer ...` to the login endpoint without other parameters. As a response you'll get a new freshly issued token (again in the Authorization header of the response).\n\ni.e\n\n```\ncurl -v -X POST \"http://{dspace-server.url}/api/authn/login\" -H \"Authorization: Bearer eyJhbG...COdbo\" -H",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/dspace-7-rest-contract/blocks/prose-s033-json-web-token-structure",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "JSON Web Token structure",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s033-json-web-token-structure.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### JSON Web Token structure\nThe JWT contains the following claims\n\nclaim | description\n--- | ---\neid|Contains the id of the eperson\nsg | Contains the id's of the special groups to which a user belongs\nexp | Contains the expiration date when a token will expire",
