      "target": "../sections/s038-using-short-lived-token.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "### Using short lived token\n\nThe request parameter below can be used for nearly every REST endpoint to perform it with authentication but without needing the authentication header:\n* **authentication-token**: optional parameter that authenticates a user, a token needs to be requested from the [following endpoint](authentication.md#Request-short-lived-token) \n\nThe following endpoints are not allowed to use the authentication-token:\n* **POST /api/authn/login**: refreshing your long-lived authentication header is not allowed using the short lived token\n* **POST /api/authn/shortlivedtokens**: crea",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
